{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-generation-completeness","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:generation-completeness","kind":"theorem","title":"Generation completeness: all embeddable knots are reachable","tags":["completeness","skein","unknotting","genus","generation","spectral-filter","embeddability"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.generation_completeness","text":"generation-completeness.md","leanSource":"generation-completeness.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:generation-completeness\"></a><p>Every knot embeddable in Bring's surface is reachable from the generator set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{G}</code> by Skein operations alone. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> be any knot with Seifert genus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g(K) \\leq 4</code>. Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> is reachable from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{G}</code> by a finite sequence of Skein crossing changes. The generation scheme produces every knot type that admits a localized knot structure in the Descartes universe.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/generation-completeness.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"8.12.10","page":"b/thm-generation-completeness","qa":{"counts":{"pass":89,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":77},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.generation_completeness","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/generation-completeness.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
